{interval, select,
                        monthly {New monthly total}
                        yearly {New yearly total}
                        other {New total}
                      }

I’ve just finished setting you up. Here’s what you know about me:
{lines}

{goal}

I haven’t connected any tools yet, so work only from what I told you — don’t try to look anything up. Reply right away with one line saying what you’re about to do, then write the first pass and put it in a document I can open, share and edit — create a file for it (or an artifact, if you can’t make files here), named for the task, with the full draft inside, not a summary of it. Rough and fast beats polished and late: headings and bullets are plenty; I want something to react to within a couple of minutes. In the chat, just say it’s ready and name the two or three things you most want my take on. Finish with two other things from my week you could take on next, and which tool I could connect to make each one better.

Keep every update to a line or two.

translation:
我刚刚完成了对你的设置。以下是你对我的了解：
{lines}

{goal}

我还没有连接任何工具，所以请只根据我告诉你的内容工作，不要试图查找任何东西。请立即用一行字回复你接下来要做什么，然后写出初稿，并放进一个我可以打开、分享和编辑的文档中：为它创建一个文件（如果这里无法创建文件，就用 Artifact），以任务命名，里面放完整的草稿，而不是摘要。又快又粗糙胜过精致但迟到：有标题和要点就足够了，我希望几分钟内就有东西可以回应。在聊天中，只需说明已经准备好，并列出你最希望我给意见的两三个点。最后再提两件你接下来可以处理的我这周的事，以及我可以连接哪个工具让每件事做得更好。

每次更新都控制在一两行。

